  "evidence_id": "THV1-20260903-global-accounting-allocation-projection-v2",
  "created_date": "2026-09-03",
  "claim_scope": "Candidate C9c-2 (both P38 reviews): the projection derives the certificate from one exact GlobalEconomicStateV1 and REFUSES with a closed code wherever V1 state does not determine a certificate the checker can accept. The previous cut claimed the projection never yields a certificate failing a row, aggregate or derived-root check: that was FALSE (an OPEN terminal over-claiming its entitlement, two terminals over-claiming together, a claimant with no entitlement, and entitlements exceeding custody all derived certificates the checker must reject) and it was VACUOUS where it was measured, because every row-bearing fixture state has all lanes disabled and the maximum row count across all twenty-nine projected fixture certificates was zero. The family now separates UNDETERMINED (more than one accepted certificate exists: the AMBIGUOUS codes) from UNRECONCILABLE (none exists: TERMINAL_WITHOUT_ENTITLEMENT, TERMINAL_EXCEEDS_ENTITLEMENT, NEGATIVE_RESIDUAL, ROW_TOTAL_OVERFLOW, NO_LANE_FOR_ROWS, MULTIPLE_ENABLED_LANES), every one of the ten codes has a test, and the byte-for-byte witness claim is re-made over a witness whose receipt actually proved a custody row, so it is no longer a statement about an empty witness.",
  "change_kind": "assurance_infrastructure",
  "risk_class": "critical",
  "invariant_ids": [
    "GAAC-PROJECTION-DERIVES-ROWS-FROM-STATE",
    "GAAC-PROJECTION-REFUSES-UNDETERMINED-SHAPES",
    "GAAC-PROJECTION-WITNESS-ADDS-ONLY-BINDING-ROOT",
    "GAAC-PROJECTION-REJECT-IS-VALUE"
  ],
  "failure_modes": [
    "a projection guesses a terminal row's control domain when the state names two candidates",
    "a projection splits the residual controlled atoms across two pending obligations arbitrarily",
    "a projection substitutes the lane state root for a witnessed lane's receipt root",
    "a projection places rows on a lane the state has not enabled, or across two enabled lanes",
    "a projection mutates or aliases the caller's state"
  ],
